{"type":"say","text":"Thank you all for your thorough reports. Let me summarize the key findings before I record the final approval. Ms. Patel, your pilot found that the package requires 90 minutes of intervention per week, not the 60 minutes currently in the draft plan. Mr. Green, the license requires the exact attribution statement 'Adapted from OpenMath Core' on every modified print or digital item. Ms. Torres, 22 eighth-grade students need a Spanish-English mathematics glossary, which is not currently listed in the package. And Mr. Brooks, the grant provides $6,800 and requires the approval record to identify it as the funding source. These are all significant findings. Before I proceed with the final approval, I want to confirm: are there any objections to approving the OpenMath Core package with the following adjustments — updating the intervention time to 90 minutes per week, ensuring a Spanish-English mathematics glossary is included for the 22 students, identifying the instructional-materials grant as the funding source at $6,800, and ensuring the attribution requirement is met on any modified materials?"}
```

